        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-11T20:43:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This accounts for the case where the spreading was done via the computed window. Basically, the default is to set the spreading by the odr. But, we also check the window between the first data-\u003etimestamp in the staged FIFO and the fifo_staged.read_ts (which is the first time motion_sense_fifo_stage_data was called after a previous commit). The window / (count - 1) gives us the spreading period which if smaller than the sensor\u0027s collection_rate will be used. Because of this, it\u0027s possible that we might have predicted the next ts to be at time N + 8ms but the real sample came in at N + 10ms. In this case, we use that or to reset our baseline timestamp for spreading.",
      "parentUuid": "9645e630_b03a9033",
      "revId": "b2f9b108d2132a83b3ff075a6aca8a4dbba23615",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
